From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: JD Daniels <jd@greenlightdata.ca>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 23:26:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-modeset: free the semaphore surface callback record
 when the waiter is already signalled

nvKmsKapiRegisterSemaphoreSurfaceCallback() allocates the callback
record before asking RM to register a waiter. When RM returns
NVOS_STATUS_ERROR_ALREADY_SIGNALLED it has not stored the record, and
the function neither frees it nor hands it back to the caller, so it
leaks.

nvidia-drm takes this path for every semaphore surface fence whose GPU
work completes before the waiter is registered, i.e. most composited
frames on a compositor that waits its render fence before each commit.
It shows up as unreclaimable kmalloc-64 slab growing at frame rate
(upstream PR 1368).

Free the record on that return. nvKmsKapiFree(NULL) is fine when no
callback was requested.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi-sync.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi-sync.c b/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi-sync.c
index 1b243d64..0d81a958 100644
--- a/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi-sync.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-modeset/kapi/src/nvkms-kapi-sync.c
@@ -445,6 +445,11 @@ nvKmsKapiRegisterSemaphoreSurfaceCallback(
         }
         return NVKMS_KAPI_REG_WAITER_SUCCESS;
     case NVOS_STATUS_ERROR_ALREADY_SIGNALLED:
+        /*
+         * No waiter was registered, so neither the callback nor
+         * unregisterSemaphoreSurfaceCallback() will ever free cb.
+         */
+        nvKmsKapiFree(cb);
         return NVKMS_KAPI_REG_WAITER_ALREADY_SIGNALLED;
     default:
         break;
